{
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Noise Riser",
 "category": "Effects",
 "text": "Sound: the rising white-noise sweep that builds tension before a drop in big beat, rave and techno: hold a key and it climbs for eight seconds.\n\nHow it's built: white noise through the State-Variable filter's band-pass; an envelope with an eight-second ATTACK sweeps the CUTOFF up (CV at 6 octaves) while a second, slightly quicker envelope fades the volume in. A Reverb for size.\n\nPlay: hold one key for the build, let go at the drop.\n\nTweak: the sweep envelope's ATTACK (the length of the build), the filter's RESONANCE (more is whistlier), the reverb's MIX.",
